From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:49:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sqlite: fdsan when built for Android

The unix VFS tags the descriptors it opens with fdsan and closes them
with the tag only under __BIONIC__ (and API level >= Q). A device
build against another C library that provides bionic's fdsan API
defines __ANDROID__ but not __BIONIC__: its database fds stay
untagged. Treat __ANDROID__ like __BIONIC__ at these guards in the
built amalgamation (sqlite-default). No change for Soong variants:
device builds define both, linux_bionic defines __BIONIC__.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no Soong variant defines __ANDROID__ without __BIONIC__]
Patch-Reason: the guards are compiled inside libsqlite, out of reach of the launcher, loader and environment; defining __BIONIC__ instead would change the libc++ ABI on glibc
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: blessing
 dist/sqlite-autoconf-3440300/sqlite3.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dist/sqlite-autoconf-3440300/sqlite3.c b/dist/sqlite-autoconf-3440300/sqlite3.c
index 84b28a102f575bf56efdc6a492f68049b628c957..9a37e10784c0ddd8f5dfa036fb471e4e5bdede11 100644
--- a/dist/sqlite-autoconf-3440300/sqlite3.c
+++ b/dist/sqlite-autoconf-3440300/sqlite3.c
@@ -38035,7 +38035,7 @@ SQLITE_PRIVATE int sqlite3KvvfsInit(void){
 # include <sys/mount.h>
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__BIONIC__)
+#if defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 # include <android/fdsan.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -38648,7 +38648,7 @@ static int robust_open(const char *z, int f, mode_t m){
     osFcntl(fd, F_SETFD, osFcntl(fd, F_GETFD, 0) | FD_CLOEXEC);
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__BIONIC__) && __ANDROID_API__ >= __ANDROID_API_Q__
+#if (defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)) && __ANDROID_API__ >= __ANDROID_API_Q__
     uint64_t tag = android_fdsan_create_owner_tag(
         ANDROID_FDSAN_OWNER_TYPE_SQLITE, fd);
     android_fdsan_exchange_owner_tag(fd, 0, tag);
@@ -39233,7 +39233,7 @@ static int unixLogErrorAtLine(
 ** and move on.
 */
 static void robust_close(unixFile *pFile, int h, int lineno){
-#if defined(__BIONIC__) && __ANDROID_API__ >= __ANDROID_API_Q__
+#if (defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)) && __ANDROID_API__ >= __ANDROID_API_Q__
   uint64_t tag = android_fdsan_create_owner_tag(
       ANDROID_FDSAN_OWNER_TYPE_SQLITE, h);
   if( android_fdsan_close_with_tag(h, tag) ){
